# Service & Repository Patterns

## Service

- `@Service`, constructor-injected repository
- Accept/return DTOs — map via `{Entity}Mapper` internally
- Throw `ResourceNotFoundException.forResourceWithId("User", id)` for missing ids
- Throw `IllegalArgumentException` for invalid query params (use `StringUtils.requireNonBlank`)
- Set server-managed fields (`id = null`, `createdAt`) in service, not controller

```java
// GOOD — 404 from service
public UserResponse findById(Long id) {
    User user = userRepository.findById(id)
        .orElseThrow(() -> ResourceNotFoundException.forResourceWithId("User", id));
    return UserMapper.toResponse(user);
}

// BAD — Optional to controller for 404
public Optional<User> findById(Long id) { ... }
```

## Repository

- Interface extending `CrudRepository<Entity, Long>` + `@Repository`
- PostgreSQL-specific SQL in `@Query` text blocks (quote reserved table names, e.g. `"user"`)
- Derived query methods for simple lookups (`findByMobileNo`)
- FK references on entities: `AggregateReference<RelatedEntity, Long>`

## Not yet adopted

- `@Transactional` (add when multi-step writes appear)
- Service interfaces (concrete classes until multiple impls needed)
